                <pb facs="0630" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2730</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-18T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                                1918, 5 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1982. Your 1313, September 12, 3 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d644-f1"/> The
                    Counselor of the Embassy presented this matter yesterday in conversation with
                    Mr. Balfour who said in substance that he entirely shared the views you set
                    forth, which the British Chargé d’Affaires in Washington had also already
                    conveyed to him by telegraph. He also said that even before he had received
                    Barclay’s communication of your views he had taken vigorous steps to mend
                    matters at Archangel both as to the future action of General Poole and to
                    correct the bad impression the occurrence had made on the Russians as far as
                    possible. He specially wished you to know of his immediate action, and said that
                    in addition to this he had repeated Barclay’s telegram textually to Lindley at
                    Archangel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
